# UI work — reproduce the design, do not reinterpret it

Read `docs/DESIGN-SYSTEM.md` before touching any UI. The full contract is there;
this is the short version.

`references/design-source/design-markup.html` has every value inline. Trace what
you write back to it.

## Forbidden without an explicit instruction in the task

- redesign cards or change their composition
- change spacing, radii, or the type scale
- change navigation or screen order
- substitute colours, or add any colour outside the palette
- **add a grey** — every muted tone is sage or bone at an alpha
- introduce a new component style
- add gradients, shadows, or effects not in the source
- change the typography hierarchy
- rename, re-case, or rewrite label text
- invent content, metrics, or affordances

If the design appears wrong, say so and stop. Do not fix it silently.

## Palette — the only colours in the app

```
--bone     #F2EFE2   primary text, key figures
--green    #00F5A5   primary accent, live/healthy, active nav
--ink      #0D0D12   base background, text on green/gold
--sage     #A6C9B4   muted text and hairlines — ALWAYS at alpha
--gold     #E3BB72   warning, amber band, offline
--red      #FF4A3D   critical, negative variance, waste
--charcoal #1B1B24   card and panel surface
--venom    #08B078   mid-green gradient stop
```

`--red` is `#FF4A3D`. It is **not** `#ff5d5d`.

## Typography

- **Anton** — big numbers and screen titles only, always weight 400.
- **Oswald** — all UI caps, labels, data lines, metrics, nav. Weights 400, 500,
  600, **700**. All four must be loaded; `font-synthesis: none` is set globally,
  so an unloaded weight renders wrong rather than falling back.
- **Archivo** — body copy and sentence-case descriptive text only. 400, 600.

**Casing:** the design's data vocabulary is UPPER CASE — `BAR 1`, `HEALTHY`,
`COUNT DUE`, `TOTAL STOCK`, `48 BOTTLES`. Sentence case appears only in Archivo
body copy and item names. Do not re-case label text.

**Tracking:** Oswald caps always carry letter-spacing. Micro caps `0.16em`,
section eyebrows `0.2em`, data caps `0.08–0.12em`. It is never zero.

## Radii

The design's vocabulary is soft: `18px` cards, `16px` alerts, `15px` metric
grids, `14px` rows and buttons, `12px` small controls, `999px` pills, `44px`
frame. A flow screen built on 3–7 px radii is wrong.

## Material

Surfaces are **glass**, not flat — the design has 51 `backdrop-filter`
declarations. Panels are translucent over a three-layer ambient gradient field.
The live dot pulses. See `docs/DESIGN-SYSTEM.md` for the exact declarations.

## Navigation

`back()` **pops the navigation stack** — it does not go home. Tab presses reset
the stack. A hardcoded `<Link to="/">` on a flow screen is a defect. Toasts
expire after 2600 ms.

## Definition of done for a UI task

1. Every value traced to `design-markup.html` or `design-script.jsx`.
2. The screen renders from the **fixture repository**, not from literals.
3. Compared against `references/ui/<screen>.png` at 390×844.
4. Tap targets at least 44×44 px; focus indicators intact.

Point 2 is load-bearing. A screen that hardcodes the design's sample figures can
pass a screenshot comparison while being entirely non-functional — that is
exactly how this project's previous design QA certified two broken screens.
